//? Title: VQA:human questions,masked tensors and explicit optimizers
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A complete CNN plus masked-LSTM teaching model answers genuine human VQA-v2 questions attached to original COCO photos. Explicit SGD count references,three independently optimized modality models,coverage-aware metrics and actual held-out inputs reveal dataset shortcuts and the limits of this small fit.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/vqa_baseline.cpp`.

> The method

Keep whole photographs and human questions source-disjoint,fit token/answer vocabularies only on fitting images,and train soft ten-answer cross-entropy. Freeze recurrent memory after each observed sequence length,then compare independently fitted joint,image-only and question-only graphs. All numerical preparation,forward/loss/optimization,metrics and plotted values use tensors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/vqa_baseline_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/vqa_baseline_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/vqa_baseline_concept.tikz > build/vqa_baseline_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/vqa_baseline_concept.svg build/vqa_baseline_concept.dvi > build/vqa_baseline_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
