> Separate unimodal models reveal dataset shortcuts

The image encoder centers RGB by.5 and uses three blocks of two3x3 SAME
He/ReLU convolutions plus VALID2x2 pooling. A global average projects to
a tanh image code. The masked LSTM projects its final hidden state with tanh.
Joint fusion concatenates image,question and their elementwise product,
then uses a tanh hidden dense layer and linear finite-answer logits.
No pretrained encoder,BN or dropout is hidden in the model.

The source full configuration uses base64,embedding300,hidden256,fusion512.
The compact fit uses8/32/32/64. Both retain all three CNN blocks and24 shared
recurrent steps. The native suite runs full and compact backward,all24
joint learned leaves and both modality gradients. Question-only and image-only
models omit the unused encoder and train independent stores. They are not
zero-input evaluations of a jointly trained graph.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  std::print("| graph | mode | learned values | learned leaves | staged activations | "
             "recurrent steps |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (bool compact : {false, true})
    for (auto mode : {m::VqaMode::kJoint, m::VqaMode::kQuestion, m::VqaMode::kImage}) {
      m::VqaConfig c;
      if (compact) {
        c.base = 8;
        c.embedding = 32;
        c.hidden = 32;
        c.fusion = 64;
      }
      n::ParameterStore p(277);
      const auto out =
          m::VqaBaseline(p, n::full({2, 64, 64, 3}, .4), n::ones({2, 24}, n::DType::Int32),
                         n::full({2}, 3., n::DType::Int32), c, mode);
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", compact ? "compact" : "full",
                 m::VqaModeName(mode), p.count(), p.size(), out.stages.size(),
                 out.question_steps.size());
    }
}
```
